# Do NOT add a bare `build/` rule here.
#
# Moodle ships *compiled* front-end assets inside directories literally named
# `build`. These are not build output that can be regenerated at will on the
# server - they are the deployed artefacts that the PHP asset endpoints read:
#   - */amd/build/*.min.js      -> lib/requirejs.php  (core_requirejs::find_one_amd_module)
#   - */yui/build/**            -> theme/yui_combo.php (core_yui_combo)
#   - lib/yuilib/*/build/**     -> YUI 2-in-3 runtime
# Ignoring them makes every git-based deployment ship without them, which
# produces "No define call for core/first", "Mismatched anonymous define()
# module" and "M.form.shortforms is not a function", and breaks Bootstrap
# tab/dropdown/modal behaviour (e.g. admin settings tab switching).
#
# Upstream Moodle only ignores generated coverage files inside those trees:
*/yui/build/*/*-coverage.js
/lib/yuilib/*/build/*/*-coverage.js
/lib/yuilib/*/*/*-coverage.js

